.vercel
limen-helix-api/node_modules/
limen-helix-api/bk-dataset.json
limen-helix-api/bk-results.json
limen-helix-api/bk_validation_results.json
helix-kernel-v4.js
.env*.local
.claude/settings.local.json
# Server-side audit log (best-effort local writes; runtime data, not source)
api/audit/reconciliation_log.jsonl
api/helix_app/audit/reconciliation_log.jsonl
# (Python bytecode is ignored tree-wide at the bottom of this file. The eight
# hand-listed api/*/__pycache__ paths that used to sit here were redundant with
# it and had to be extended by hand for every new package.)

# Node deps + local toolchain
node_modules/

# package-lock.json IS COMMITTED, deliberately. It was ignored here until
# 2026-08-01, which made `npm ci` (and setup-node's `cache: npm`) impossible:
# both refuse to run without a lockfile in the tree, so the CI workflow added on
# 2026-07-31 could never have completed a single run. Ignoring it also meant the
# dependency versions that pass locally were never the versions CI or Vercel
# resolved. A lockfile is a build input, not a build artifact.

# Local backup snapshots of refreshed data files
assets/data/command-board-data.json.before-*
assets/data/command-board-data.json.pre-validated-*

# One-shot diagnostic verifier artifacts (do not commit; runtime-only)
_verify_static_claims.py
_verify_static_claims_hits.json
_verify_pre.log
_verify_post.log
_verify_triage.log

# Runtime artifacts from the autonomic loop. REGENERATED every 6h tick.
# Committing them caused .git to balloon to 2.5GB and blew the GitHub
# Actions runner disk (Worker IOException No space left on device, 2026-05-30).
# Read paths live in Upstash Redis (UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL + _TOKEN in Vercel)
# or are recomputed on-demand from source data.
# assets/data/_vitals.json — committed: vitals.html fetches it as a static asset (un-ignored 2026-06-04, lean-first; mirrors full ce59e48)
assets/data/_engine-build-log.json
assets/data/_autonomous-regen-queue.json
assets/data/_pattern-proposals.json
assets/data/_operator-actions.json
assets/data/_k2-persist-log.json
assets/data/_ai-budget.json

# Pre-enrich + pre-redensify backups, printed packages — historical/runtime
assets/data/companies/_pre-enrich/
assets/data/companies/_pre-redensify/
assets/printed/

# 84MB build artifact — render files in treatment-discovery/ are the committed output
assets/data/treatment-discovery-cube.json

# Kernel-validation working logs (runtime, not source). Its bytecode is covered
# by the tree-wide __pycache__ rule at the bottom.
scripts/*.log
scripts/*.jsonl

# Session scratch — root-level working/diagnostic files (regenerable)
/_*.txt
/_*.cjs
/_live*.json
/_props*.json
/_snap.json
/_fstat.json
/_live_render.js
/_wip-backup/

# Generated lane DRAFT documents — keep LOCAL, never deploy (would be public at
# limenhelix.com/_fired_*.md). Patent/grant/research/spec drafts; regenerable.
/_fired*.md
/_fired-*.md
/_nsf_rewrite.md
/_sbir_rewrite.md
/_front-door-and-access-spec.md

# Side project — keep OUT of the LIMEN repo (firewall). Relocate to its own project.
/coffee-house/
scripts/reports/

# Installed Claude Code skills (npx skills add → .agents/skills, symlinked into
# Claude Code). Third-party code, local-only; never commit or deploy.
.agents/

# Raw YouTube transcript corpora (~21MB) — keep LOCAL only, never in git history.
# Regenerable via: python -m yt_dlp --skip-download --write-auto-subs --sub-langs "en.*" <channel>/videos
# The distilled maps in docs/research/*.md ARE committed (the irreplaceable synthesis).
docs/research/torti-transcripts-corpus.txt
docs/research/saraev-transcripts-corpus.txt

# Enriched town lead lists (scripts/enrich-town.mjs) - real business contact
# data, NEVER commit to this PUBLIC repo.
assets/data/town-*.csv

# Ad-hoc curl scratch from endpoint debugging (raw response headers + fetched page
# dumps, ~800KB of them). Regenerable in one command; never source. Root-anchored so
# a real file of the same name in a subdirectory is still tracked normally.
/body.html
/head.txt
/lh.txt
/nh.txt
/live.html
/l2.html

# NOT ignored (2026-07-31): organ-master-brain and organ-bridge audit the FRESHNESS of
# _master-inbox.json and _bridge-build-log.json. While these were ignored, CI could never see
# them, so the daily pulse silently skipped both staleness checks. Measured on the full tree at
# the time of tracking: bridge readings 1130h stale (47 days), master inbox 1429h (59 days) —
# neither had ever appeared in the operator queue. Tracked so the audit can actually run.
# Same precedent as assets/data/_vitals.json, which has always been tracked and committed.

# Python bytecode caches, anywhere in the tree. Three were tracked before the
# per-directory rules above existed; git keeps tracking a file even after it is
# ignored, so those needed git rm --cached. These two patterns cover any future
# directory without needing a new line each time.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Headless Chrome user-data profiles, left behind by the screenshot/video runs.
# 11MB each and they contain Default/Login Data, Default/Network/Cookies and Trust
# Tokens — browser credential stores. This repo's source is publicly readable and
# main auto-deploys, so these must never be tracked. Regenerable: Chrome rebuilds a
# profile on next launch.
/cp_*/

# Screenshots produced by those same runs. Regenerable output, not source.
/shots/
